{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDE5L1RoZSUyMFNuYWlsJTIwQW5kJTIwVGhlJTIwV2hhbGUlMjAlMjgyMDE5JTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"The Snail And The Whale","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/qWsqdJ6XUvwimqxwlplIazKjpve.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/vCQFdqOYhRdSdLl5wqKXSDUchwA.jpg","description":"A half hour animated film for all the family based on the much-loved book written by Julia Donaldson and illustrated by Axel Scheffler.  The Snail and the Whale is the much loved classic that shows us a restless young snail who has ambitions to travel the world. The other snails think she should stay put, but she puts out a call for a “Lift wanted around the world”. Eventually her call is answered by a great big grey-blue humpback whale! She sets off with him across the seas. On their journey the snail and the whale discover towering icebergs and far-off lands, fiery mountains and golden sands. The snail is delighted by the wonderful world around her, until she realises how small it makes her feel.\n\nRated G · Released 21 Oct 2020 · United Kingdom · Language: English · 26 min\nStudio: Magic Light Pictures\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2019","genres":["Animation","Family","TV Movie","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.6","imdb_id":"tt9303756","moviedb_id":655424,"tmdbId":655424,"runtime":"26 min","cast":["Rob Brydon","Sally Hawkins","Diana Rigg","Cariad Lloyd","Max Lang"],"director":["Max Lang","Daniel Snaddon"],"writer":["Suzanne Lang","Max Lang"],"released":"2020-10-21T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"\"How I long to sail!\" said the tiny snail.","country":"United Kingdom","language":"English","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Max Lang","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/7yVJMJhG8dDb6winBdM7cUxcbqG.jpg"},{"name":"Rob Brydon","character":"Whale (voice)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/xoKLZVwzaUgTUEvPX4vymXpC1fU.jpg"},{"name":"Sally Hawkins","character":"Snail (voi